implementationPlan.note:
Created scripts/local-runner/certify-bridge.mjs (100 lines). It exports BRIDGE_BOUNDS, CERTIFY_PAYLOAD (plus a private PAYLOAD_SHA256), certifySnapshot, watchedSession and BRIDGE_CHECKS, per the plan.

watchedSession resolves the frozen { outcome, exitCode, exit, stdout, overflow, broken }. R13e's exitCode contract (the architect comment) is passed straight through from runCheckSession. Inside the wrapped spawn it:
- wraps child.kill to record a local kill;
- registers its own 'close' recorder;
- tees stdout through its own decoder and parseGuestFrame, keeping stdout output only, bounded by limit (overflow), with onStdout after each frame;
- treats any throw as broken; the handler never throws.

Two defensive `?.` reads (context.provider ?? {}, context.bounds?.x) make a malformed context reject only with runCheckSession's fixed CHECK_SESSION_INPUT_INVALID, never a codeless TypeError.

certifySnapshot passes CERTIFY_PAYLOAD directly: validateImport already copies each file's bytes (readEntry: new Uint8Array(data)), so a Buffer.from copy would be redundant. Comparisons use the private digest, so mutating the export can only fail a check.

Test fix: CB3's broken-frame row now sends the bad frame in its own chunk. createFrameDecoder.push throws mid-chunk and drops that chunk's earlier frames, so one combined write lost the 'ok' frame. That is test-fixture timing, not a runtime defect.

